FIX: Set a lifespan to automatically destroy the unique 'hitbox' after the attack duration
(400ms is a safe value for the 2-frame animation at 200ms per frame, 500ms allows for some delay)</comment><value name="mySprite"><block type="variables_get" id="xt7o4}hY#*dF-S:[F[x;"><field name="VAR" id="n%t[,+fBS!lk]YDLeVme">hitbox</field></block></value><value name="value"><shadow type="math_number" id="PQG:IzJ#Mw=bt(KZi%]j"><field name="NUM">500</field></shadow></value><next><block type="variables_set" id="wO*l0Qk2k^zgwxJEt|f,"><field name="VAR" id="SwJy4lPF#W^ggo%7nNVg">EnemyAttacking</field><comment pinned="false" h="80" w="160">--- 4. COOLDOWN SETUP ---
These flags should be set when the attack *finishes*, not when it starts.
It's recommended to move these inside a timer.after call based on animation duration.
